            <h2>What Are Ergonomic Alternative Office Chairs?</h2>
            <p>Ergonomic alternative office chairs break the mold of conventional desk seating. Instead of locking your body into a static 90-degree angle, they encourage active sitting — subtle, continuous micro-movements that keep your muscles engaged, your posture upright, and your focus sharper throughout the day. The two most popular types are saddle stools and kneeling chairs, both designed with decades of Scandinavian ergonomic research behind them.</p>

            <h3>Kneeling Chair vs Standard Office Chair</h3>
            <p>A kneeling chair like the Variable Balans distributes your weight between the seat and shin pads, tilting your pelvis forward to create an open hip angle. This naturally aligns your spine into its standing posture — even while seated. Standard office chairs, by contrast, encourage a collapsed 90° hip angle that compresses spinal discs and weakens core muscles over time. If you spend 6+ hours at a desk, a kneeling chair offers a fundamentally better sitting mechanic.</p>

            <h3>Are Saddle Stools Good for Office Work?</h3>
            <p>Saddle stools like the Varier Move are purpose-built for elevated surfaces — standing desks, kitchen islands, drafting tables, and adjustable workstations. The convex wooden base allows 360° tilt, meaning your body naturally finds balance through constant small adjustments. This prevents the stiffness that comes from sitting in one position for hours. For those who alternate between standing and sitting throughout the day, a saddle stool is the ideal companion to a height-adjustable desk.</p>

            <h3>Which Ergonomic Office Chair Is Right for Your Home Office?</h3>
            <p>For a standard-height home office desk, the Variable Balans kneeling chair is the better fit — it's compact, tucks under most desks, and encourages focus-friendly posture. For a standing desk or elevated workstation, the Varier Move saddle stool is purpose-built for that environment. Both are lightweight enough to move between rooms, making them versatile additions to any home workspace.</p>
